{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795431080,"nonce":"MeRULZJnG9yMvuSvpy5lFuz8hK0=","title":"demo-oracle deploy.sh: role preflight loses the kubectl attach race and refuses a good image","message":"Seen 2026-11-23 deploying the demo to 0.7.2.\n\ndeploy/demo-oracle/deploy.sh preflight_run() runs `kubectl run --rm --restart=Never --attach --quiet` with `scarab-server --role __scarab_preflight__`. With the image already in containerd's cache, the container exits (clap error, exit 2) before kubectl attaches, so the captured output is only \"pod scarab/scarab-preflight-server terminated (Error)\". The script then refuses: \"could not determine which roles … supports\".\n\nThe image was fine: `docker run --platform linux/arm64 ghcr.io/thulasi-ram/scarab-server:0.7.2 --role __x__` prints \"[possible values: converged, api, scheduler, executor, webhook, workspace]\". Rerunning deploy.sh passed.\n\nFix: do not depend on attach. Create the Pod without --rm/--attach, wait until it reaches a terminated phase (kubectl wait --for=jsonpath='{.status.phase}'=Failed|Succeeded, with the 300s pull timeout), read `kubectl logs`, then delete it. A pull failure still surfaces, because the Pod never terminates and the wait times out, and the message should say so.\n\nAcceptance: the preflight reads the role list on a warm cache every time; a missing or unpullable tag still refuses with a message naming the pull.","files":null}]}